# React component patterns

- Functional components only.
- Colocate a feature's pieces: a block type's `schema.ts`, `grade.ts`, `Component.tsx`, `report.ts`,
  and `editorDescriptor.tsx` all live together in `src/blocks/<type>/` — don't scatter them by
  "type of file" across the tree.
- Extract a custom hook when stateful logic (e.g. heartbeat sending, autosave debouncing) is used
  by more than one component.
- Prefer composition over prop-drilling, especially for MDXEditor's `JsxComponentDescriptor`
  editors — build small nested editor components rather than one giant props object.
- Name components after what they render, not their file location (`QuizComponent`, not `Index`).

```tsx
// BAD — logic and markup for two concerns tangled together
function ChapterPage() { /* fetch + heartbeat + render all inline */ }

// GOOD
function useHeartbeat(chapterId: string) { /* ... */ }
function ChapterPage() {
  useHeartbeat(chapterId);
  return <ChapterReader ... />;
}
```
